  "notes": [
    "Transport: OSC to MagicQ; the module tracks playback, execute and DBO state itself because MagicQ does not report OSC-driven changes back, so feedbacks reflect what Companion sent plus console-reported manual fader moves (comments in actions.js and feedbacks.js).",
    "Playbacks are limited to 1-10 and execute pages to 1-10, execute numbers to 1-1000 (src/constants.js MAX_EXEC_PAGE, MAX_EXEC_NR; parsePlayback and parseExecTarget in src/main.js). The limits are enforced in the callbacks, not by the option definitions; labels show the ranges after resolving the constants.",
    "Number-like fields are text inputs with useVariables, not number fields. The regex values are the resolved @companion-module/base constants (Regex.NUMBER, Regex.SIGNED_NUMBER, Regex.FLOAT_OR_INT) and are informational.",
    "Dropdowns and the exeToggle checkbox set disableAutoExpression; text inputs stay expression-capable.",
    "Variables (pb1-pb10, pb<N>_flash, exec<page>_<nr>) and presets are not catalogued. Execute variables are created at runtime as executes are seen.",
    "Built on @companion-module/base ~2.0.4: expressions are supported for option values (derived from the base major version, not tested against a running Companion)."
  ]
